# Task Management — Secure Messaging App

---

## ✅ Project Rules
- One-to-one private messaging only  
- Windows desktop only  
- No accounts, no sign-ins, no backups  
- Messages must always stay encrypted  

---

## 👥 Team
- **Cesar** → Focus on **encryption (security) and networking (sending messages)**  
- **Luke** → Focus on **user interface (UI) and local storage (saving chats)**  

---

## 📌 Phase 1 — Encryption (Cesar)
Tasks:  
- [ ] Create a way for the app to generate a **private key** (like a digital ID)  
- [ ] Make sure each message is **locked (encrypted)** before it leaves the device  
- [ ] Make sure messages can be **unlocked (decrypted)** by the other person only  
- [ ] Test sending a sample message between two apps  

**Goal:** Messages can be sent securely without anyone else reading them.  

---

## 📌 Phase 2 — Networking (Cesar)
Tasks:  
- [ ] Let two computers connect directly (peer-to-peer)  
- [ ] If direct connection doesn’t work, add a simple “relay” that just passes along encrypted messages (it can’t read them)  
- [ ] Handle errors (lost connection, retry)  

**Goal:** Two computers can talk to each other in real time.  

---

## 📌 Phase 3 — User Interface (Luke)
Tasks:  
- [ ] Build a **chat window** with text box and send button  
- [ ] Add a **public key exchange screen** (QR code or copy/paste text)  
- [ ] Show when a message is sent/received  
- [ ] Add a simple settings screen (view your public key)  

**Goal:** A normal user can send and receive messages easily.  

---

## 📌 Phase 4 — Local Storage (Luke)
Tasks:  
- [ ] Decide if messages are saved on the computer or disappear when the app closes  
- [ ] If saved, make sure they are **stored encrypted** (locked)  
- [ ] Add an option to clear all stored messages  

**Goal:** Messages saved on the device remain private.  

---

## 📌 Phase 5 — Security & Testing (Both)
Tasks:  
- [ ] Double-check that no plaintext (unlocked messages) ever leave the device  
- [ ] Try to “hack” the app by intercepting messages (should be unreadable)  
- [ ] Make sure nothing sensitive is saved in logs or temporary files  

**Goal:** Prove the app is truly private.  

---

## 📌 Phase 6 — Release (Both)
Tasks:  
- [ ] Package the app into a Windows installer (.exe)  
- [ ] Write a **Quick Start Guide** for normal users  
- [ ] Publish the app on GitHub Releases  

**Goal:** Anyone can download, install, and start using the app.  

